Smallest positive float  : 2.225074E-308 
Smallest deviation from 1: 2.220446E-16 

In D3d we have 3 states beloning to the a1g, eg and eg irriducible representation
This gives us 4 parameters related to the energy of the 3 states and the mixing between the two states belonging to the eg irriducible representation
We label the two eg states as egpi and egsigma
If Ea1g = Eegpi and Eegmix=0 one has cubic symmetry
In order to define the orientation of the crystal we list the direction of the C3 and C2 axis belonging to the D3d pointgroup
We furthermore list the direction of the C4 axis one obtains if Ea1g = Eegpi and Eegmix=0
Even for cases where the axis of the D3d pointgroup are the same we still have two different orientations related to how one branches from Oh to D3d
:-)
